    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The lands comprise an old stone ruin set on c. 4.1 Acres of good quality lands with mature natural boundaries and exceptional scenery overlooking the surrounding sloping countryside and wider rural landscape. The ruins are positioned towards the roadside and are surrounded by a number of mature trees, creating a sheltered and attractive setting within the lands.\r\n\r\nThe holding is laid out in a single division and is currently in grass, suitable for a range of agricultural uses including grazing or hobby farming. The lands benefit from established hedgerows which provide both privacy and natural shelter, while also enhancing the overall character of the property.\r\n\r\nThe property enjoys good road frontage and benefits from existing vehicular access directly from the public road. The elevated nature of the lands provides pleasant views over the surrounding countryside while still maintaining a sense of privacy.\r\n\r\nOverall, the property would make a superb setting for a one-off rural dwelling subject to the necessary planning permission. Alternatively, the lands would also be suitable for use as a small farm holding, equine use or lifestyle property given the quality of the ground, road access and attractive rural setting.\r\n\r\nLOCATION\r\nBarrack Road is situated in the rural village of Glencullen, in the Dublin Mountains to the south of Dublin City. The area sits on the slopes of Two Rock Mountain along the R116 regional route.\r\n\r\nBarrack Road runs just outside the centre of Glencullen village and enjoys a quiet countryside setting with panoramic views across the surrounding hills and valleys. Despite its rural character, the area is easily accessible, located just a short drive from Enniskerry, Stepaside, Kilternan and Sandyford, while the M50 motorway and Dundrum Town Centre are within convenient commuting distance.\r\n\r\nThe locality is well known for its scenic landscape and outdoor amenities, forming part of the wider Dublin Mountains recreation area, which offers numerous walking, cycling and hiking trails. The road also lies close to the renowned Johnnie Fox’s Pub, one of Ireland’s oldest and most famous traditional pubs, which acts as a focal point for the village."
      },
